### Layer Relationships

```
L1 (Identity) ← Informs technical depth for L2, validates L3 domain expertise
    ↓
L2 (Preferences) ← Learned from L4 patterns, shapes content presentation
    ↓
L3 (Interests) ← Clustered themes feed into L4 project detection
    ↓
L4 (World Context) ← Recent activity, references L3 clusters, triggers L5
    ↓
L5 (Interest Cards) ← Ephemeral, highest priority for immediate responses
```

**Inheritance rules:**
- L5 cards can override L2 preferences for content length (e.g., deep research → longer responses)
- L4 projects contextualize L3 interests (e.g., "Rust interest" + "RAG project" → focus on async/performance)
- L1 occupation validates L3 confidence scores (e.g., high confidence in ML for a SWE is credible)

